H8000.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7999 (שָׁלַם);
to complete, to restore
KJV: deliver, finish.

H8001.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7965 (שָׁלוֹם);
prosperity
KJV: peace.

H8002.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
properly, requital, i.e. a (voluntary) sacrifice in thanks
KJV: peace offering.

H8003.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
complete (literally or figuratively); especially friendly
KJV: full, just, made ready, peaceable, perfect(-ed), quiet, Shalem (by mistake for a name), whole.

H8004.definition:
the same as H8003 (שָׁלֵם); peaceful;
Shalem, an early name of Jerusalem
KJV: Salem.

H8006.definition:
the same as H8005 (שִׁלֵּם);
Shillem, an Israelite
KJV: Shillem.

H8007.definition:
probably for H8008 (שַׂלְמָה); clothing;
Salma, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Salma.

H8008.definition:
transp. for H8071 (שִׂמְלָה);
a dress
KJV: clothes, garment, raiment.

H8009.definition:
the same as H8008 (שַׂלְמָה); clothing;
Salmah, an Israelite
KJV: Salmon. Compare H8012 (שַׂלְמוֹן).

H8010.definition:
from H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); peaceful;
Shelomah, David's successor
KJV: Solomon.

H8011.definition:
feminine of H7966 (שִׁלּוּם);
