KJV: recompense.

H8012.definition:
from H8008 (שַׂלְמָה); investiture;
Salmon, an Israelite
KJV: Salmon. Compare H8009 (שַׂלְמָה).

H8013.definition:
feminine plural of H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); pacifications;
Shelomoth, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Shelomith (from the margin), Shelomoth. Compare H8019 (שְׁלֹמִית).

H8014.definition:
from H8008 (שַׂלְמָה); clothed;
Salmai, an Israelite
KJV: Shalmai.

H8015.definition:
from H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); peaceable;
Shelomi, an Israelite
KJV: Shelomi.

H8016.definition:
patronymically from H8006 (שִׁלֵּם);
a Shilemite (collectively) or descendants of Shillem
KJV: Shillemites.

H8017.definition:
from H7965 (שָׁלוֹם) and H410 (אֵל); peace of God;
Shelumiel, an Israelite
KJV: Shelumiel.

H8018.definition:
or שֶׁלֶמְיָהוּ; from H8002 (שֶׁלֶם) and H3050 (יָהּ); thankoffering of Jah;
Shelemjah, the name of nine Israelites
KJV: Shelemiah.

H8019.definition:
or שׁלוֹמִית; (Ezra 8:10), from H7965 (שָׁלוֹם); peaceableness;
Shelomith, the name of five Israelites and three Israelitesses
KJV: Shelomith.

H8020.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Shalman, a king apparently of Assyria
KJV: Shalman. Compare H8022 (שַׁלְמַנְאֶסֶר).

H8021.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
a bribe
KJV: reward.

H8022.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Shalmaneser, an Assyrian king
KJV: Shalmaneser. Comp H8020 (שַׁלְמַן).

H8023.definition:
