H8033.definition:
a primitive particle (rather from the relative pronoun, H834 (אֲשֶׁר));
there (transferring to time) then; often thither, or thence
KJV: in it, [phrase] thence, there (-in, [phrase] of, [phrase] out), [phrase] thither, [phrase] whither.

H8034.definition:
a primitive word (perhaps rather from through the idea of definite and conspicuous position; compare H8064 (שָׁמַיִם));
an appellation, as amark or memorial of individuality; by implication honor, authority, character
KJV: [phrase] base, (in-) fame(-ous), named(-d), renown, report.

H8035.definition:
the same as H8034 (שֵׁם); name;
Shem, a son of Noah (often includ. his posterity)
KJV: Sem, Shem.

H8036.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8034 (שֵׁם)
{an appellation, as amark or memorial of individuality; by implication honor, authority, character}
KJV: name.

H8037.definition:
from H8074 (שָׁמֵם); desolation;
Shamma, an Israelite
KJV: Shamma.

H8038.definition:
apparently from H8034 (שֵׁם) and H83 (אֵבֶר); name of pinion, i.e. illustrious;
Shemeber, a king of Zeboim
KJV: Shemeber.

H8039.definition:
perhaps for H8093 (שִׁמְעָה);
Shimah, an Israelite
KJV: Shimah. Compare H8043 (שִׁמְאָם).

H8040.definition:
or שְׂמֹאל; a primitive word (rather perhaps from the same as H8071 (שִׂמְלָה) (by insertion of the aleph) through the idea of wrapping up);
properly, dark (as enveloped), i.e. the north; hence (by orientation), the left hand
KJV: left (hand, side).

H8041.definition:
a primitive root (denominative from H8040 (שְׂמֹאול));
to use the left hand or pass in that direction)
KJV: (go, turn) (on the, to the) left.

H8042.definition:
from H8040 (שְׂמֹאול);
situated on the left side
KJV: left.

H8043.definition:
for H8039 (שִׁמְאָה) (compare H38 (אֲבִיָּם));
