KJV: (laid, [idiom] most) desolate(-ion), waste.

H8079.definition:
probably from H8074 (שָׁמֵם) (in the sense of poisoning);
a lizard (from the superstition of its noxiousness)
KJV: spider.

H8080.definition:
a primitive root;
to shine, i.e. (by analogy) be (causatively, make) oily or gross
KJV: become (make, wax) fat.

H8081.definition:
from H8080 (שָׁמַן);
grease, especially liquid (as from the olive, often perfumed); figuratively, richness
KJV: anointing, [idiom] fat (things), [idiom] fruitful, oil(-ed), ointment, olive, [phrase] pine.

H8082.definition:
from H8080 (שָׁמַן);
greasy, i.e. gross; figuratively, rich
KJV: fat, lusty, plenteous.

H8083.definition:
